<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49237" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trĭumphātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who triumphs</i>, <i>a triumpher</i>, <i>conqueror</i>, <i>vanquisher</i>
			(post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de Samnitibus triumphator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 285, 12</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Reg. 15,
			29</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Triumphator, an epithet of Jupiter, App. de Mundo, 75,
			10.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Of Hercules,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 1042</span></i>
			.—Of the Roman emperors, <i><span class="en">Inscr.
				Orell. 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">erroris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Min. Fel. Oct. 37</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
